            <ArticleTitle>Testicular Ischemia Due to a Band Around the Spermatic Cord.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/2156-7514.157856</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of an 18-year-old boy who was admitted to our hospital with a 2-day history of pain in the right scrotum. Ultrasound examination showed signs of ischemia, with dampened testicular arterial flow and bell-clapper deformity. Surgery revealed a constricting fibrous band around the distal spermatic cord resembling the bell-clapper deformity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
